+# CLAUDE.md
+
+This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.
+
+## Commands
+
+```bash
+# First-time setup (install, .env, key, migrate, npm build)
+composer run setup
+
+# Start full dev environment (server + queue + logs + vite, all concurrent)
+composer run dev
+
+# Run tests
+composer run test
+
+# Run a single test file or filter
+php artisan test --filter=TestClassName
+
+# Lint / format with Pint
+./vendor/bin/pint
+
+# Run migrations
+php artisan migrate
+
+# Tinker REPL
+php artisan tinker
+```
+
+## App concept
+
+**3tab** — users have a public profile at `/{username}` where anyone can send them an **Atab**: an anonymous (or named) emotional/complaint message. The platform surfaces received atabs and supports conversation threads.
+
+## Architecture
+
+### Models
+
+- **`User`** — standard auth model extended with `username`, `bio`, `mood`, `allow_anonymous`. Route key is `username`. Has many `Atab`s as recipient.
+- **`Atab`** — a message sent to a user. Fields: `recipient_id` (required FK → users), `sender_id` (nullable FK → users), `body`, `is_anonymous` (bool, default true), `mood` (sender's emotional state). The `getSenderNameAttribute()` accessor resolves to "Anonymous" when appropriate.
+
+### Routing convention
+
+All user-facing routes use `/{username}` as the base segment. A `->where('username', '[a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+')` constraint prevents collisions with reserved paths.
+
+### Views
+
+Views use inline Tailwind/CSS with a Vite fallback: if `public/build/manifest.json` exists, Vite assets load; otherwise inline `<style>` is rendered. This pattern is used in all Blade templates.
+
+### Key files
+
+| Path | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `routes/web.php` | All web routes |
+| `app/Http/Controllers/ProfileController.php` | Public profile page |
+| `resources/views/profile/show.blade.php` | Profile + atab feed + send form |
+| `database/migrations/` | Schema — run in chronological order |
+
+### Database
+
+SQLite by default (see `.env.example`). The `atabs` table uses `nullOnDelete()` for `sender_id` so deleting a sender preserves the atab record.
